    "result_text": "Done. Tests remain green.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Main finding \u2014 locality triplication (agreed, fixed):**\n- Added a `default String locality(Owner owner)` helper on `OwnerMapper` wrapping `CustomerCode.regionOf(owner.getCustomerCode())`.\n- The `locality` mapping, the `timezone` mapping (nested), and `ownerSegment` now all call `locality(owner)` instead of repeating the inline derivation. `ownerSegment` now composes two helpers symmetrically (`membershipLevel(owner)` + `locality(owner)`), matching the `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel` idiom. This removes all three copies of the inlined expression.\n\n**Minor observation \u2014 `isKnownRegion` source of truth (agreed with the lighter option):**\n- I kept `REGION_POSTCODES.containsKey(region)` rather than introducing a fourth encoding of the region set (a dedicated canonical set would itself have to be kept in sync with the three existing pinned maps, trading one redundancy for another). Instead I added a comment noting that all three maps are pinned to the same region set and that the postcode map is the chosen source of truth, addressing the \"reads arbitrarily\" concern the reviewer raised.\n\nAll acceptance behaviour is unchanged: `./mvnw test` passes (`STANDARD_METRO` and `STANDARD_REGIONAL` cases green).",
